Site Report: Kor-road, Bori Metropolis.

The subsurface at this station comprises four layers with resistivity values of 1916, 1252, 1658, and 581 ohm-m. Analyzing the layers in depth order, the first triplet (1916, 1252, 1658) follows an H-type pattern (r1 > r2 < r3), while the second triplet (1252, 1658, 581) follows a K-type pattern (r1 < r2 > r3). This results in a combined curve type of HK. This calculated classification is consistent with the survey interpretation currently on file.

